oordinator alone shared interfaces/metadata/integration. No dependencies/download/install/network, unsafe/new sys boundary, C shim, unsupported OS code, staging/commit/delete/reset, recursive agents or broad UI/E2E/fuzz/performance campaign. Mac13+ AppleSilicon only, MPL2, no GPL-editor source or external SVG fetch. Explicit ownership/lifetimes, bounded input/checked arithmetic/fallible significant allocations. Source<800lines; split before exceeding. No TODO/unimplemented/mock production paths for named scope. If needed contract is absent, stop with concrete dependency rather than narrowing scope or editing peer crate. Every named C public API/helper mapped in parity-map.json to symbols/tests/limits/ownership/errors/exact safe adaptations; preserve meaningful assertions, not only is_err checks.\n\n# Execution and verification\nOnly /Users/megasoft78/Desktop/Freelance/vexel/.worktrees/rust6-css; Standard subscription Luna High, one writer. Read OWNER-DIRECTIVES/AGENTS/order; use accepted source contracts.\ncargo +stable check -p vexel-svg-css --locked --offline\ncargo +stable test -p vexel-svg-css --locked --offline\npython3 scripts/wo_validate.py WO-RUST-SVG-CSS-01 --ready\npython3 scripts/ledger.py validate ledger.jsonl\ngit diff --check\nExact existing Rust1.99/macOS13, repo-local Cargo/cache/tmp/targets, no fmt/clippy install or claim.\n\n# Output\nUncommitted candidate, result<=400words, parity-map.json/verification.txt with exact checks/adaptations/failures/remaining downstream work. Independent review, preservation audit and named main checks required before acceptance. Existing subscription allowance only; no purchased credits/API billing. Stop/checkpoint on allowance/rate errors, no retry loop.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
